## Explanation

I implemented efficient and secure data persistence using two different Object-Relational Mapping (ORM) tools depending on the project stack: **SQLAlchemy** (Python) for the UA Arcade Cabinet project and **Prisma ORM** (TypeScript/PostgreSQL) for the RepairCafé Ticketing System.

---

### 1. Python & SQLAlchemy (UA Arcade Cabinet)

For the backend of the UA Arcade Cabinet, I used SQLAlchemy to model games and dynamic asset overrides.

#### Model Definitions
We defined structured relationships between games, uploaded packages (`ZipUpload`), and custom asset replacements:

```python
class Game(Base):
    __tablename__ = 'game'
    id: Mapped[UUID] = mapped_column(primary_key=True, default=uuid4)
    name: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(120))
    description: Mapped[Optional[str]] = mapped_column(String(2000), nullable=True)
    is_active: Mapped[bool] = mapped_column(default=True)
    zip_uploads: Mapped[list['ZipUpload']] = relationship(back_populates='game')
    assets: Mapped[list['Asset']] = relationship(back_populates='game')
```
*   **Link**: [database.py](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-UAnt-007-Arcade-cabinet/blob/main/code/backend/src/database/database.py#L47-L61)

#### Database Operations
To execute safe queries, I injected the database session as a dependency in FastAPI routers and used standard session operations:

```python
@router.post('/', dependencies=[Depends(get_api_key)])
def create_game(request: GameCreateRequest, db: Session = Depends(database.get_session)):
    new_game = database.Game(
        name=request.name,
        description=request.description,
        is_active=request.is_active
    )
    db.add(new_game)
    db.commit()
```
*   **Link**: [game.py (Create Game Router)](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-UAnt-007-Arcade-cabinet/blob/main/code/backend/src/game/game.py#L59-L79)

